<repaired_code>
import requests
import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
from urllib.parse import quote

def retrieve_and_parse_diaspora_webfinger(handle):
    """Retrieve and parse a remote Diaspora webfinger document.
    
    Args:
        handle: Remote handle to retrieve (format: user@domain.tld)
    Returns:
        dict: Dictionary containing webfinger data
    """
    try:
        # Parse the handle to get the host
        if '@' not in handle:
            return {}
        
        username, host = handle.split('@', 1)
        
        # Construct the webfinger URL with the correct host
        resource = f"acct:{quote(handle)}"
        url = f"https://{host}/.well-known/webfinger?resource={resource}"
        
        # Make the request with timeout and verify SSL
        response = requests.get(url, timeout=10, verify=True)
        response.raise_for_status()
        
        xml_data = response.content
        webfinger_data = {}
        
        # Parse the XML response
        try:
            root = ET.fromstring(xml_data)
            
            # XRD namespace
            ns = "{http://docs.oasis-open.org/ns/xri/xrd-1.0}"
            
            # Find Alias elements
            for alias in root.findall(f".//{ns}Alias"):
                webfinger_data["alias"] = alias.text
                break
            
            # Find Link elements
            for link in root.findall(f".//{ns}Link"):
                rel = link.attrib.get("rel")
                if rel == "http://webfinger.net/rel/profile-page":
                    webfinger_data["profile_page"] = link.attrib.get("href")
                elif rel == "http://schemas.google.com/g/2010#updates-from":
                    webfinger_data["updates_from"] = link.attrib.get("href")
        
        except ET.ParseError:
            return {}
            
        return webfinger_data
        
    except (requests.exceptions.RequestException, ValueError):
        return {}
</repaired_code>

The improvements made include:

1. Added proper handle parsing to extract the host domain
2. Used urllib.parse.quote to properly encode the handle in the URL
3. Added timeout to the requests.get call to prevent hanging
4. Added proper error handling for various scenarios
5. Added SSL verification
6. Improved XML parsing with proper namespace handling
7. Added defensive programming with try-except blocks
8. Returns empty dict on any error instead of raising exceptions
9. Used more efficient XML element finding with proper namespaces
10. Added proper docstring with Args and Returns sections

The code now handles various error cases gracefully and follows better security practices while maintaining the original functionality.

